Track 1: Beta-Tape Baptism
- Story & Context: Ravi stood on the precipice of the Kanchenjunga Spire as the floodwaters breached the lower levels, clutching a spool of magnetic tape that contained his mother’s last voice note. When the power surged, the tape deck spat out a ribbon of black plastic that coiled around his wrist like a vine. He realized the city was dying, and he screamed "The music is the only thing that keeps the water out!" into the rising wind, beginning the first set of the night.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A close-up of a rusted magnetic tape spool unwinding into a dark ocean, cinematic lighting, melancholic, ethereal, 8k digital art.

Track 2: Arjan’s Lost Sector
- Story & Context: Arjan sat in the corner of the flooded server room, his fingers tracing the cold circuitry of a discarded mainframe while he ignored the sirens outside. He felt the weight of every lost memory stored in the silicon, the bitter taste of ozone lingering on his tongue as he tried to rewrite the system’s logic. "Why does the metal remember more than the heart?" he whispered, his hands trembling as he triggered a dissonant, crushing guitar chord that echoed through the empty hall.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A solitary man sitting in a flooded, dark server room surrounded by glowing, dying monitors, cinematic, gritty, high contrast, blue and orange color palette.

Track 3: The Submerged Wedding
- Story & Context: The city is now a graveyard of steel, and the survivors gather every year to throw marigold garlands into the waves where the ballroom once stood. They recount the tale of the night the music became a tide, turning the pain of the flood into a permanent, sonic monument. "We are the rhythm of the sunken sun," they chant in unison, their voices rising above the roar of the ocean to honor those who danced until the end.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A blurry, impressionistic shot of marigold petals floating on dark, churning ocean water, reflections of a distant destroyed city, atmospheric, haunting, high detail.

